        "event_narrative": "Multiple reports of two waterspouts were made from members of the public via social media. The first waterspout was very skinny_ nearly vertical_ and a spray ring was visible when it reached the mature stage. The first waterspout lasted approximately 6 minutes. As the first waterspout reached the mature stage_ a second waterspout developed close by from the same parent cell. The second waterspout initially was nearly vertical and skinny as well_ but tilted to a 45-degree angle and grew thicker as it reached the mature stage. The second waterspout lasted approximately 10 to 12 minutes_ and dissipated before reaching land."
